==German==

===Etymology 1===
Probably a [[pars pro toto]] expression, from a very old root (related to Ancient Greek {{term|φαλλός||penis|tr=phallos|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}), with the related meaning "ball".

====Noun====
{{de-noun|g=m|genitive=Bullen|plural=Bullen}}

# [[bull|Bull]] (male cattle).

===Etymology 2===
From ''(Land)Puller'', a non-derogatory term for a policeman of the 18th century. In the 1960s, the term ''Bullen'' was first used by politically left protesters, possibly associating the American derogatory term ''[[pig]]'' of that time with the animal ''[[bull]]''.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|g=m|genitive=Bullen|plural=Bullen}}

# (derogatory) Male [[cop]].

=====Related terms=====
* [[Bullette]]

===Etymology 3===
From {{etyl|la}} ''[[bulla]]'' "seal capsule", originally meaning "ball, bullet".

====Noun====
{{de-noun|g=f|plural=Bullen}}

# [[bull|Bull]] (papal decree).

=====Related terms=====
* [[Bulette]]

